{
  "description": "Average-cost inventory (P24, U-157 to U-160) shared by the engine (packages/shared/fixtures/inventory-golden.json) and the ClientLedger client (fixtures/inventory/golden.json, byte-identical; the --demo engine runs every case not marked engineOnly). Synthetic. Dates are 2026; quantities are 4-place strings, money 2-place strings, average costs 6-place strings. Values are signed by their effect on the inventory asset account: a receipt is positive, a sale's relief negative, a negative-stock correction C is shown as -C.",
  "rules": [
    "Position: (date, sortRank, transaction created_at, transaction id); restatements have sortRank 0, every other movement 1. An edit keeps created_at.",
    "State per item: Q on hand, P posted value (the GL), T true value, L = round6(T/Q) after the latest row that left Q > 0 and T > 0 (the true last positive average).",
    "Outflow at cost of q > 0 units (sale, quantity-only adjustment down), on T: Q > 0 and q <= Q: relief = round2(T x q / Q); q > Q: relief = (Q > 0 ? T : 0) + round2(excess x c), excess = q - max(Q, 0), c = L if L > 0, else the item's purchase cost when the line was posted, else 0.",
    "Inflow at cost of r units (customer return, quantity-only adjustment up): round2(T x r / Q) if Q > 0, else round2(r x c).",
    "Given value: a receipt adds its line amount, a vendor return takes its line amount off, an adjustment with a value adds that value.",
    "Correction when Q < 0 before an inflow of r units worth A: k = min(r, -Q); C = round2(A x k / r) - round2(-T x k / -Q), posted on the inflow's document (Dr COGS, Cr inventory when C > 0); T := T + A - C.",
    "Residual: a row leaving Q = 0 with T != 0 moves T to the item's COGS account on that document.",
    "round2 and round6 are half away from zero at 40 digits, negatives included (round2(5.015) = 5.02, round2(-0.005) = -0.01).",
    "Closed periods (engineOnly cases): rows dated on or before the closing date keep their posted values unless they belong to the document posted under the closing-date password; the difference P - T lands in a system cost restatement dated closing + 1, one per (trigger, item), Dr/Cr inventory vs the item's COGS account. An open restatement re-values to T - P on every walk; at 0 it is voided.",
    "NEGATIVE_STOCK {itemId, date, onHand} warns on the first row per item whose running quantity newly goes below 0; posting is allowed.",
    "Every case starts from an empty company with the seed accounts and items, or from the end state of the case named in `from`. `expect` after a step lists the item's state after that step; `rows` lists every movement row after the case's last step, in position order. Keys and cases marked engineOnly are not checked by the demo engine."
  ],
  "seed": {
    "accounts": {
      "inventory": { "name": "Inventory Asset", "type": "asset", "detailType": "other_current_asset", "systemTag": "inventory_asset" },
      "cogs": { "name": "Cost of Goods Sold", "type": "cogs", "detailType": "cost_of_goods_sold" },
